/-! # Smooth points of the stack of curves and unobstructed deformations

Source: Stacks Project, moduli-curves.tex, Tag 0DZU, lemma-in-smooth-locus,
and the preceding coefficient-ring choice
(blueprint: lem-sfb-curve-smooth-locus-deformation-test).

The curve groupoid, its full open substacks and the marked Artinian coefficient
category are the existing constructions. Flat scheme deformations are expressed
by their actual special-fibre pullback squares, without further finiteness conditions.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.ProperCurveModuli

/-- Every field has a coefficient ring of the indicated form, with its residue map.
In characteristic zero the residue map identifies the coefficient ring with the field;
in positive characteristic the ring is Cohen with that residue characteristic.
Source: Stacks, moduli-curves.tex, paragraph preceding Tag 0DZU
(blueprint: lem-sfb-curve-smooth-locus-deformation-test).

Proof (step 2 of the node): in characteristic zero use the field itself and its
identity residue map. In positive characteristic use lem-weil-pbc-cohen-rings-exist
and the specified isomorphism of the quotient by p with the field. A Cohen ring is
a local PID, hence Noetherian; its maximal ideal is generated by p. -/
theorem exists_curve_coefficient_ring (k : Type u) [Field k] :
    ∃ (Λ : Type u) (_ : CommRing Λ) (_ : IsLocalRing Λ) (_ : IsNoetherianRing Λ)
      (_ : Algebra Λ k),
      Function.Surjective (algebraMap Λ k) ∧
      RingHom.ker (algebraMap Λ k) = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal Λ ∧
      ((ringChar k = 0 ∧ Function.Bijective (algebraMap Λ k)) ∨
        (0 < ringChar k ∧ IsCohenRing (ringChar k) Λ)) := by
  sorry

/-- The largest smooth open of the curve stack detects exactly unobstructed marked
flat scheme deformations, for every permitted coefficient ring and every proper
scheme of dimension at most one. Membership is the existence of a curve object
representing the given scheme over its specified field and lying in the full open.
The lifting arrow `l` identifies the reduction with the original deformation; the
special-fibre marking of the lift is `j ≫ l`, so it extends the given marking.
Source: Stacks, moduli-curves.tex, Tag 0DZU, lemma-in-smooth-locus
(blueprint: lem-sfb-curve-smooth-locus-deformation-test).

Proof following the six steps of the node:
1. Curve descent and representability of Isom spaces
   (lem-sfb-curve-descent-isom-spaces) give a stack. With the assumed diagonal and
   atlas it is algebraic. Curve limit preservation (lem-sfb-curve-limit-preservation)
   and lem-sfb-stack-limit-preserving-lfp give local finite presentation. Apply
   lem-sfb-stack-maximal-smooth-open to obtain the largest smooth full open.
2. The coefficient choice is exists_curve_coefficient_ring. Any allowed ring is
   Noetherian and torsion-free over Z: in mixed characteristic p is a nonzero
   uniformizer and primes different from p are units. Apply
   lem-weil-pbc-pid-torsion-free-module-flat to see that the coefficient base is flat.
3. An Artinian local test has nilpotent maximal ideal by
   lem-weil-pbc-artinian-local-noetherian-nilpotent. A flat scheme deformation is
   proper by lem-sfb-proper-nilpotent-base-change-reflection and locally finitely
   presented by lem-sfb-flat-deformation-lfp (use pqf-lem-lft-fp-locnoeth on the
   proper special fibre). Properness gives quasi-compactness and a quasi-compact
   diagonal, hence finite presentation. All geometric fibres are field extensions
   of the special fibre, of dimension at most one by lem-pc-dim-base-change.
4. Conversely a marked curve-space deformation is a scheme by
   lem-sfb-thickening-of-scheme-space. Its special fibre is a nilpotent thickening.
   The two marked deformation groupoids have the same objects, isomorphisms and
   cartesian restrictions, including the specified reduction across a surjection.
5. Base change the curve stack to the flat coefficient base. Descent is componentwise;
   its diagonal and atlas base change using lem-sfb-stack-chartwise-smooth-etale-calculus.
   The flat-base-change clause of lem-sfb-stack-maximal-smooth-open identifies its
   smooth open with the pullback of the original one. The two membership conditions
   pull back the same open to Spec k. Curve limit preservation and
   lem-sfb-stack-limit-preserving-lfp give local finite presentation over the coefficient
   base as well, hence local finite type.
6. Apply lem-sfb-stack-artinian-smoothness-criterion at the residue point. This point
   is a finite-type closed immersion into the coefficient spectrum. Step 4 identifies
   its marked lifts with the flat scheme lifts written below, preserving and reflecting
   unobstructedness; step 5 identifies membership with the original smooth open.
No lci, isolated-singularity, connectedness or nonemptiness hypothesis is used. -/
theorem exists_curve_smooth_open_deformation_test
    (hdiagonal : HasAlgebraicSpaceDiagonal (category (Spec (.of (ULift.{u} ℤ)))))
    (hatlas : ∃ (U : Over (Spec (.of (ULift.{u} ℤ))))
      (a : BasedFunctor (discreteModuli (yoneda.obj U))
        (category (Spec (.of (ULift.{u} ℤ))))),
      IsSmoothModuliAtlas (category (Spec (.of (ULift.{u} ℤ)))) U a) :
    ∃ M : OpenModuliSubstack (category (Spec (.of (ULift.{u} ℤ)))),
      IsSmoothModuliStack M.category ∧
      (∀ N : OpenModuliSubstack (category (Spec (.of (ULift.{u} ℤ)))),
        IsSmoothModuliStack N.category → N.IsContainedIn M) ∧
      ∀ (k Λ : Type u) [Field k] [CommRing Λ] [IsLocalRing Λ] [IsNoetherianRing Λ]
        [Algebra Λ k],
        Function.Surjective (algebraMap Λ k) →
        RingHom.ker (algebraMap Λ k) = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal Λ →
        ((ringChar k = 0 ∧ Function.Bijective (algebraMap Λ k)) ∨
          (0 < ringChar k ∧ IsCohenRing (ringChar k) Λ)) →
        ∀ (X : Scheme.{u}) (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of k)),
          IsProper f → topologicalKrullDim X ≤ 1 →
          ((∃ C : ProperCurveFamily
              (Over.mk (specULiftZIsTerminal.from (Spec (.of k)))),
            ∃ e : C.space.obj.obj ≅ yoneda.obj
                (Over.mk (f ≫ specULiftZIsTerminal.from (Spec (.of k)))),
              e.hom ≫ yoneda.map (Over.homMk
                (U := Over.mk (f ≫ specULiftZIsTerminal.from (Spec (.of k))))
                (V := Over.mk (specULiftZIsTerminal.from (Spec (.of k)))) f rfl) =
                  C.projection ∧
              M.property ⟨Over.mk (specULiftZIsTerminal.from (Spec (.of k))), C⟩) ↔
            ∀ (A' A : ArtinDeformation.TestCategory Λ k) (q : A' ⟶ A),
              Function.Surjective (ArtinDeformation.map q) →
              ∀ (Y : Scheme.{u}) (g : Y ⟶ Spec (.of (ArtinDeformation.ring A)))
                (j : X ⟶ Y),
                Flat g →
                IsPullback j f g
                  (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (ArtinDeformation.residue A).toRingHom)) →
                ∃ (Y' : Scheme.{u})
                  (g' : Y' ⟶ Spec (.of (ArtinDeformation.ring A'))) (l : Y ⟶ Y'),
                  Flat g' ∧ IsPullback l g g'
                    (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (ArtinDeformation.map q).toRingHom))) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.ProperCurveModuli
